{"kind":"request","text":"C+D legacy transport needs two bounded contract decisions before implementation. The reviewed proposal4a3faa17 and independent peer946692da confirm that no existing API closes either gap. First, choose whether an authenticated local receiving entry, its exact FactUse, content-checked retained bytes, recorded kind and retained producer may enter a separate runtime retained-use arm. It must not become Fetched, Source, CheckedSequence, from.pin or a genuine-only Native/capability projection; caller-supplied Entry scalars alone cannot authenticate it. The alternative needs separately funded remote-birth retention; fetching births after restart adds forbidden I/O. Second, confirm the required per-invocation owner hook: compare an in-memory commit generation and closed-group lifetime, invalidated only from existing successful commit/head notifications. SqliteStore.scope and PreparedRead.current add reads and cannot serve as a free callback. Direct Scope and archive/rebuild notification coverage must be explicit, with no optional fallback or new SELECT. Own.sequence can carry a genuine token admitted from pinned()'s existing stored(0) read; no extra birth read, but bounded admission CPU and append-before-fold handling remain owed. Please rule on those representation and owner-hook contracts. All C+D heads remain separate, unassembled and unvalidated.","body":{"conditions":"Choose the bounded retained-use provenance contract and required no-extra-SQL owner hook, including genuine Own token carry from the existing birth read. Preserve all current Native/capability trust restrictions, cap-A bounds, deadlines and no-extra-I/O rules. No implementation or result is claimed.","no_git_artifact":"true","peer_sha256":"946692da3363fc0d05c99f757d579fd58015e7afcbf91dbfeb8897bb9afb95b6","source":"/private/tmp/artroom-cd-legacy-transport-own-retained-owner-proposal-v1-20261112/SOURCE.READY.json","source_sha256":"4a3faa178f3f42a9261a7177bc8edccf2868dff1c480d3543f